text:
Pasal 2
Pemberdayaan Perempuan dan Perlindungan Anak dilaksanakan  berdasarkan asas:
a. penghormatan terhadap hak-hak perempuan dan anak;
b. kesetaraan dan keadilan gender;
c. non-diskriminasi;
d. kearifan lokal;
e. kepentingan yang terbaik bagi perempuan dan anak;
f. penegakan dan kepastian hukum; dan
g. Penghargaan terhadap pendapat anak.

translated_text:
Article 2
The Empowerment of Women and Protection of Children is implemented based on the principles of:
a. respect for the rights of women and children;
b. gender equality and justice;
c. non-discrimination;
d. local wisdom;
e. the best interests of women and children;
f. law enforcement and legal certainty; and
g. respect for the views of the child.

text:
Pasal 3
Peraturan Daerah ini bertujuan:
a. menjamin terpenuhinya hak perempuan dan anak di daerah;  b. mencegah terjadinya tindakan, keputusan dan kebijakan yang melanggar  hak perempuan dan anak;
c. menghapus segala bentuk kekerasan dan eksploitasi terhadap  perempuan dan anak;
d. melindungi, memberi rasa aman bagi korban tindak kekerasan;  e. memberikan pelayanan kepada korban kekerasan; dan
f. menyelenggarakan pemulihan secara menyeluruh kepada korban kekerasan.

translated_text:
Article 3
This Regional Regulation aims to:
a. guarantee the fulfillment of the rights of women and children in the region;
b. prevent the occurrence of actions, decisions and policies that violate the rights of women and children;
c. eliminate all forms of violence and exploitation against women and children;
d. protect and provide a sense of security for victims of violence;
e. provide services to victims of violence; and
f. carry out comprehensive recovery for victims of violence.

text:
Pasal 4
Ruang lingkup pengaturan Pemberdayaan Perempuan dan Perlindungan  Anak meliputi:
a. peningkatan kualitas hidup perempuan;
b. perlindungan perempuan dan anak;
c. peningkatan kualitas keluarga;
d. sistem data gender dan Anak;
e. pemenuhan hak Anak;
f. pembinaan dan pengawasan; dan
g. pembiayaan.

translated_text:
Article 4
The scope of regulation for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection includes:
a. improvement of women's quality of life;
b. protection of women and children;
c. improvement of family quality;
d. gender and Child data system;
e. fulfillment of Child rights;
f. guidance and supervision; and
g. financing.

text:
Pasal 5
(1) Dalam rangka meningkatkan kualitas hidup perempuan, Pemerintah  Daerah bertanggung jawab :
a. menghormati dan menjamin hak perempuan tanpa diskriminasi sesuai dengan harkat dan martabat kemanusiaan;
b. melaksanakan Pengarusutamaan Gender di Daerah;
c. membentuk pokja Pengarusutamaan Gender di Daerah;
d. meningkatkan Pemberdayaan Perempuan dalam peran, kualitas dan  kemampuan dibidang;
1. politik;
2. hukum;
3. sosial; dan
4. ekonomi.
e. menguatkan dan mengembangkan lembaga penyedia layanan  Pemberdayaan Perempuan di Daerah;
(2) Tanggungjawab Pemerintah Daerah dalam upaya peningkatan kualitas  hidup perempuan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dilaksanakan  oleh OPD sesuai dengan tugas dan fungsinya.

translated_text:
Article 5
(1) In order to improve the quality of life of women, the Regional Government is responsible for:
a. respecting and guaranteeing the rights of women without discrimination in accordance with human dignity;
b. implementing Gender Mainstreaming in the Region;
c. establishing a Gender Mainstreaming working group in the Region;
d. enhancing Women's Empowerment in roles, quality and capacity in the fields of:
1. politics;
2. law;
3. social; and
4. economy.
e. strengthening and developing service provider institutions for Women's Empowerment in the Region;
(2) The responsibility of the Regional Government in efforts to improve the quality of life of women as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented by OPD in accordance with their duties and functions.

text:
Pasal 9
Pokja Pengarusutamaan Gender Daerah sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal  5 ayat (1) huruf c mempunyai tugas:
a. mempromosikan dan memfasilitasi Pengarusutamaan Gender kepada  masing-masing OPD;
b. melaksanakan sosialisasi dan advokasi Pengarusutamaan Gender kepada  Camat, dan Wali Nagari;
c. menyusun program kerja setiap tahun;
d. mendorong terwujudnya perencanaan dan penganggaran yang Responsif  Gender;
e. menyusun rencana kerja pokja Pengarusutamaan Gender setiap tahun; f. bertanggung jawab kepada Bupati melalui Wakil Bupati; g. merumuskan rekomendasi kebijakan pengarusutamaan gender kepada  Bupati;
h. menyusun profil Gender Daerah;
i. melakukan pemantauan pelaksanaan Pengarusutamaan Gender dimasing-masing OPD;
j. menetapkan tim teknis untuk melakukan analisis terhadap anggaran  Daerah;
k. menyusun rencana aksi daerah tentang Pengarusutamaan Gender di  Daerah; dan
l. mendorong dilaksanakannya pemilihan dan penetapan focal point dimasing-masing OPD.

translated_text:
Article 9
The Regional Gender Mainstreaming Working Group as referred to in Article 5 paragraph (1) letter c has the following duties:
a. promoting and facilitating Gender Mainstreaming to each OPD;
b. conducting socialization and advocacy of Gender Mainstreaming to Sub-district Heads and Wali Nagari;
c. preparing work programs every year;
d. encouraging the realization of Gender Responsive planning and budgeting;
e. preparing the work plan of the Gender Mainstreaming working group every year;
f. being responsible to the Regent through the Vice Regent;
g. formulating gender mainstreaming policy recommendations to the Regent;
h. preparing the Regional Gender profile;
i. monitoring the implementation of Gender Mainstreaming in each OPD;
j. establishing a technical team to conduct analysis of the Regional budget;
k. preparing a regional action plan on Gender Mainstreaming in the Region; and
l. encouraging the implementation of selection and determination of focal points in each OPD.

text:
Pasal 11
(1) Focal Point Pengarusutamaan Gender pada setiap OPD sebagaimana  dimaksud dalam Pasal 9 huruf l terdiri dari pejabat dan/atau staf yang  membidangi tugas perencanaan dan/atau program.
(2) Focal Point Pengarusutamaan Gender sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat  (1), mempunyai tugas:
a. mempromosikan Pengarusutamaan Gender pada unit kerja;
b. memfasilitasi penyusunan rencana kerja dan penganggaran OPD yang  responsif gender;
c. melaksanakan pelatihan, sosialisasi, advokasi Pengarusutamaan  Gender kepada seluruh pejabat dan staf di lingkungan OPD; d. melaporkan pelaksanaan Pengarusutamaan Gender kepada pimpinan  OPD;
e. mendorong pelaksanaan analisis gender terhadap kebijakan, program,  dan kegiatan pada unit kerja; dan
f. memfasilitasi penyusunan data gender pada masing-masing OPD; (3) Focal Point Pengarusutamaan Gender sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat  (1), dipilih dan ditetapkan oleh pimpinan OPD.

translated_text:
Article 11
(1) The Gender Mainstreaming Focal Point at each OPD as referred to in Article 9 letter l consists of officials and/or staff in charge of planning and/or program duties.
(2) The Gender Mainstreaming Focal Point as referred to in paragraph (1), has the following duties:
a. promoting Gender Mainstreaming in the work unit;
b. facilitating the preparation of work plans and budgeting of OPD that are gender responsive;
c. implementing training, socialization, advocacy of Gender Mainstreaming to all officials and staff within the OPD environment;
d. reporting the implementation of Gender Mainstreaming to the leadership of the OPD;
e. encouraging the implementation of gender analysis on policies, programs, and activities in the work unit; and
f. facilitating the preparation of gender data at each OPD;
(3) The Gender Mainstreaming Focal Point as referred to in paragraph (1), is selected and determined by the leadership of the OPD.

text:
Pasal 12
Upaya peningkatan peran, kualitas dan kemampuan perempuan dalam  bidang politik sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 5 ayat (1) huruf d angka 1  meliputi:
a. melaksanakan sosialisasi untuk meningkatkan partisipasi politik  perempuan dalam pemilihan umum;
b. melaksanakan program yang mendorong tingkat keterlibatan perempuan  dalam proses politik dan jabatan publik;
c. melakukan fasilitasi pengembangan diri perempuan dalam berorganisasi,  berserikat dan berkumpul;
d. melibatkan perempuan dalam pengambilan keputusan yang menyangkut  kepentingan perempuan;

translated_text:
Article 12
Efforts to enhance the role, quality and capability of women in the political field as referred to in Article 5 paragraph (1) letter d number 1 include:
a. implementing socialization to increase women's political participation in general elections;
b. implementing programs that encourage the level of women's involvement in political processes and public positions;
c. providing facilitation for women's self-development in organizing, associating and assembling;
d. involving women in decision-making concerning women's interests;

text:
Pasal 13
Upaya peningkatan peran, kualitas dan kemampuan perempuan dalam  bidang hukum sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 5 ayat (1) huruf d angka  2 meliputi:
a. melakukan sosialisasi untuk meningkatkan pengetahuan dan kesadaran  hukum perempuan;
b. melakukan pemetaan dan mereview kebijakan bias gender; c. melibatkan organisasi perempuan dalam proses penyusunan dan  pembahasan produk hukum Daerah yang berkaitan dengan peran serta  perempuan;

translated_text:
Article 13
Efforts to enhance the role, quality and capability of women in the field of law as referred to in Article 5 paragraph (1) letter d number 2 include:
a. conducting socialization to increase legal knowledge and awareness of women;
b. conducting mapping and reviewing gender-biased policies; c. involving women's organizations in the process of formulating and discussing Regional legal products related to women's participation;

text:
Pasal 14
Upaya peningkatan peran, kualitas dan kemampuan perempuan dalam  bidang sosial sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 5 ayat (1) huruf d angka 3  meliputi:
a. peningkatan pengetahuan dan keterampilan untuk mendorong  pemenuhan pendidikan sesuai dengan potensi yang dimiliki; b. peningkatan dan pemenuhan kualitas kesehatan terhadap perempuan; c. peningkatan kesadaran dan pengetahuan tentang perencanaan keluarga  mandiri, sehat dan sejahtera termasuk akses layanan konsultasi dan  pencatatan perkawinan;
d. peningkatan kesadaran perempuan terhadap dampak pernikahan dini; e. memfasilitasi dan mengupayakan pelestarian adat istiadat dan  pengembangan ilmu pengetahuan, teknologi, seni dan budaya untuk  kemajuan perempuan;
f. melakukan peningkatan kesadaran dan pengetahuan perempuan  terhadap perencanaan keluarga mandiri, sehat dan sejahtera; g. melakukan program dalam menurunkan angka kematian ibu melahirkan; h. mendorong pembentukan organisasi perempuan di Daerah;

translated_text:
Article 14
Efforts to enhance the role, quality and capability of women in the social field as referred to in Article 5 paragraph (1) letter d number 3 include:
a. enhancement of knowledge and skills to encourage fulfillment of education in accordance with existing potential; b. enhancement and fulfillment of health quality for women; c. enhancement of awareness and knowledge about independent, healthy and prosperous family planning including access to consultation services and marriage registration;
d. enhancement of women's awareness of the impact of early marriage; e. facilitating and endeavoring to preserve customs and traditions and the development of science, technology, arts and culture for the advancement of women;
f. conducting enhancement of women's awareness and knowledge regarding independent, healthy and prosperous family planning; g. conducting programs to reduce maternal mortality rates; h. encouraging the establishment of women's organizations in the Region;

text:
Pasal 15
Upaya peningkatan peran, kualitas dan kemampuan perempuan dalam  bidang ekonomi sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 5 ayat (1) huruf d angka  4 meliputi:
a. melaksanakan program, kegiatan, pelatihan untuk peningkatan  keterampilan dan keahlian perempuan dalam rangka mewujudkan  peningkatan kesejahteraan perempuan;
b. fasilitasi penguatan modal usaha bagi perempuan yang memiliki ekonomi  lemah;
c. pemasaran produk hasil usaha perempuan yang memiliki ekonomi lemah; d. pelatihan pengembangan kemampuan perempuan melalui pemberdayaan  ekonomi keluarga prasejahtera;
e. pelatihan kewirausahaan kepada perempuan secara komprehensif.

translated_text:
Article 15
Efforts to enhance the role, quality and capability of women in the economic field as referred to in Article 5 paragraph (1) letter d number 4 include:
a. implementing programs, activities, training for the improvement of women's skills and expertise in order to realize the improvement of women's welfare;
b. facilitation of business capital strengthening for women with weak economic capacity;
c. marketing of products resulting from businesses of women with weak economic capacity;
d. training for the development of women's capabilities through economic empowerment of pre-prosperous families;
e. comprehensive entrepreneurship training for women.

text:
Pasal 16
(1) Peran Pemerintah Daerah dalam upaya Perlindungan Perempuan dan  Anak:
a. menetapkan dan menyelenggarakan kebijakan, program dan kegiatan  Perlindungan Perempuan dan Anak;
b. melakukan upaya pencegahan terjadinya tindak kekerasan terhadap  perempuan termasuk tindak pidana perdagangan orang;
c. meningkatkan efektivitas layanan terhadap perempuan dan Anak  korban tindak kekerasan;
d. meningkatkan upaya perlindungan terhadap tenaga kerja perempuan dan Anak;
e. menguatkan dan mengembangkan lembaga penyedia layanan  Perlindungan Perempuan dan Anak;
f. melakukan kerjasama dengan Pemerintah, Pemerintah Daerah  lainnya, pihak swasta, dunia usaha dan/atau lembaga swadaya  Masyarakat dalam upaya pencegahan terjadinya tindak kekerasan  terhadap perempuan dan Anak;
g. melibatkan peran aktif keluarga, ninik mamak, bundo kanduang,  pemuka adat, pemuka agama, Masyarakat, dan lembaga dibidang  Perlindungan Perempuan dan Anak;
(2) Peran Pemerintah Daerah dalam upaya perlindungan perempuan  sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dilaksanakan oleh OPD sesuai  dengan tugas dan fungsinya serta dapat berkoordinasi dengan instansi  terkait.

translated_text:
Article 16
(1) The role of Regional Government in the efforts of Protection of Women and Children:
a. establish and implement policies, programs and activities for the Protection of Women and Children;
b. undertake prevention efforts against acts of violence toward women including criminal acts of human trafficking;
c. increase the effectiveness of services for women and Children victims of acts of violence;
d. increase protection efforts for women and Child workers;
e. strengthen and develop service provider institutions for the Protection of Women and Children;
f. conduct cooperation with the Government, other Regional Governments, private parties, business sectors and/or community non-governmental organizations in efforts to prevent acts of violence toward women and Children;
g. involve the active role of families, ninik mamak, bundo kanduang, customary leaders, religious leaders, the Community, and institutions in the field of Protection of Women and Children;
(2) The role of Regional Government in the efforts of protection of women as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented by OPD in accordance with their duties and functions and may coordinate with relevant agencies.

text:
Pasal 18
Keluarga dalam upaya perlindungan terhadap hak perempuan berperan : a. melindungi perempuan dari konflik dan kekerasan dalam rumah tangga  yang merendahkan martabat perempuan;
b. memberikan kesempatan yang sama pada perempuan mengembangkan  diri di bidang pendidikan, sosial, ekonomi, politik dan budaya; dan c. mencegah terjadinya pelanggaran terhadap hak perempuan dalam rumah  tangga.

translated_text:
Article 18
The family in efforts to protect women's rights has the role to: a. protect women from conflict and domestic violence that degrades the dignity of women;
b. provide equal opportunities to women to develop themselves in the fields of education, social, economic, political and cultural; and c. prevent the occurrence of violations of women's rights in the household.

text:
Pasal 19
(1) Orang tua dalam upaya perlindungan terhadap hak anak berperan:  a. mengasuh, memelihara, mendidik, dan melindungi anak; b. menumbuhkembangkan anak sesuai dengan kemampuan, bakat, dan  minatnya;
c. memberikan pendidikan formal dan non formal;
d. membimbing anak berperilaku sesuai dengan agama, etika dan moral  serta adat istiadat; dan
e. mencegah terjadinya perkawinan pada usia anak.
(2) Dalam hal orang tua tidak ada, atau tidak diketahui keberadaannya, atau  karena suatu sebab, tidak dapat melaksanakan kewajiban dan tanggung  jawabnya, maka kewajiban dan tanggungjawab sebagaimana dimaksud  pada ayat (1) dapat beralih pada keluarga.

translated_text:
Article 19
(1) Parents in the effort to protect the rights of children have the role to: a. care for, maintain, educate, and protect children; b. develop children in accordance with their abilities, talents, and interests;
c. provide formal and non-formal education;
d. guide children to behave in accordance with religion, ethics and morals as well as customs; and
e. prevent marriage at child age.
(2) In the event that parents do not exist, or their whereabouts are unknown, or due to a certain reason, cannot carry out their obligations and responsibilities, then the obligations and responsibilities as referred to in paragraph (1) may transfer to the family.

text:
Pasal 20
(1) Dalam rangka mencegah terjadinya tindak kekerasan terhadap  perempuan dan anak, Pemerintah Daerah:
a. menyelenggarakan sosialisasi mengenai pencegahan kekerasan  terhadap perempuan dan anak dengan mengoptimalkan peran  lembaga adat, budaya, agama dan organisasi kemasyarakatan;
b. menyediakan pedoman tentang penanganan tindak kekerasan  terhadap perempuan dan anak;
c. melibatkan peran serta masyarakat dalam pemulihan dan reintegrasi; d. mengembangkan database dan sistem informasi yang terintegrasi  tentang tindak kekerasan terhadap perempuan dan anak;
e. mengembangkan program pemberdayaan keluarga;
f. penguatan fungsi organisasi kemasyarakatan yang bergerak dibidang  pemberdayaan perempuan dan perlindungan anak; dan
g. menyediakan fasilitas umum yang nyaman dan aman untuk  perempuan dan anak.
(2) Pencegahan terjadinya tindak kekerasan perempuan dan anak  sebagaimana dimaksud dalam ayat (1), dilaksanakan oleh OPD yang  tugas dan fungsinya di bidang :
a. sosial;
b. kesehatan;
c. pendidikan;
d. ketenagakerjaan;
e. pemberdayaan perempuan dan perlindungan anak;
f. mental dan spiritual;
g. informatika dan komunikasi; dan
h. ketentraman dan ketertiban.
(3) Pencegahan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1), dilaksanakan oleh  OPD sesuai dengan bidang tugasnya secara terpadu dan  berkesinambungan berdasarkan Rencana Aksi Daerah.

translated_text:
Article 20
(1) In order to prevent the occurrence of acts of violence against women and children, the Regional Government:
a. conducts socialization regarding the prevention of violence against women and children by optimizing the role of customary, cultural, religious institutions and community organizations;
b. provides guidelines on handling acts of violence against women and children;
c. involves community participation in recovery and reintegration; d. develops an integrated database and information system regarding acts of violence against women and children;
e. develops family empowerment programs;
f. strengthens the function of community organizations engaged in women's empowerment and child protection; and
g. provides public facilities that are comfortable and safe for women and children.
(2) Prevention of the occurrence of acts of violence against women and children as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be implemented by OPD whose duties and functions are in the fields of:
a. social affairs;
b. health;
c. education;
d. manpower;
e. women's empowerment and child protection;
f. mental and spiritual;
g. informatics and communication; and
h. peace and order.
(3) Prevention as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be implemented by OPD in accordance with their respective fields of duty in an integrated and sustainable manner based on the Regional Action Plan.

Article 21
In order to prevent acts of violence against women and Children, the community:
a. monitors various conditions occurring in its environment that may give rise to violations of the rights of women and children;
b. increases awareness of violations of the rights of women and children;
c. strengthens the role of community organizations, religious organizations and the family environment; and
d. prevents unregistered marriages and marriage at child age.

text:
Pasal 22
Dalam rangka mencegah terjadinya tindak kekerasan terhadap perempuan dan anak, orang tua dan keluarga:
a. melindungi perempuan dan anak dari berbagai pelanggaran hak dalam  rumah tangga;
b. mendorong terbentuknya keluarga yang harmonis, edukatif dan  demokratis;
c. memberikan tauladan yang baik kepada anak sesuai ajaran agama dan  adat;
d. mengawasi anak dalam beraktifitas di dalam ataupun di luar rumah; dan e. memberikan peluang bagi anak berdialog menyampaikan pendapat secara  demokratis.

translated_text:
Article 22
In order to prevent the occurrence of acts of violence against women and children, parents and family:
a. protect women and children from various violations of rights within the household;
b. encourage the formation of a harmonious, educative and democratic family;
c. provide good examples to children in accordance with religious and customary teachings;
d. supervise children in their activities inside or outside the home; and e. provide opportunities for children to engage in dialogue and express their opinions democratically.

text:
Pasal 23
(1) Dalam rangka melaksanakan Perlindungan Perempuan dan Anak di  Daerah, Pemerintah Daerah membentuk UPTD PPA sesuai dengan  ketentuan peraturan perundang-undangan.
(2) UPTD PPA berfungsi untuk memberikan layanan terhadap perempuan  dan Anak yang mengalami permasalahan pidana dan/atau perdata.  (3) Lingkup pelayanan UPTD PPA sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (2)  meliputi:
a. pelayanan pengaduan;
b. rehabilitasi kesehatan;
c. rehabilitasi sosial;
d. bimbingan rohani;
e. pendampingan;
f. penegakan dan bantuan hukum; dan
g. pemulangan dan reintegrasi sosial.
(4) Dalam melaksanakan fungsinya UPTD PPA berkewajiban: a. memberikan pelayanan dan penanganan secepat mungkin kepada  perempuan dan anak yang mengalami permasalahan;
b. memberikan kemudahan, kenyamanan, keselamatan dan bebas biaya  kepada perempuan dan anak yang mengalami permasalahan; c. menjaga kerahasiaan perempuan dan anak yang mengalami  permasalahan;
d. menjamin keadilan dan kepastian hukum bagi perempuan dan anak  yang mengalami permasalahan.
(5) UPTD PPA bertanggung jawab kepada OPD yang menyelenggarakan  urusan pemerintahan di bidang Pemberdayaan Perempuan dan  Perlindungan Anak.

translated_text:
Article 23
(1) In order to implement the Protection of Women and Children in the Region, the Regional Government establishes UPTD PPA in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.
(2) UPTD PPA functions to provide services to women and Children who experience criminal and/or civil problems.
(3) The scope of services of UPTD PPA as referred to in paragraph (2) includes:
a. complaint services;
b. health rehabilitation;
c. social rehabilitation;
d. spiritual guidance;
e. assistance;
f. enforcement and legal aid; and
g. repatriation and social reintegration.
(4) In carrying out its functions, UPTD PPA is obligated to:
a. provide services and handling as quickly as possible to women and children who experience problems;
b. provide convenience, comfort, safety and free of charge to women and children who experience problems;
c. maintain the confidentiality of women and children who experience problems;
d. guarantee justice and legal certainty for women and children who experience problems.
(5) UPTD PPA is responsible to the OPD that administers governmental affairs in the field of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection.

text:
Pasal 25
Pelayanan pengaduan sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 23 ayat (3) huruf  a dapat dikoordinasikan oleh UPTD PPA dengan instansi terkait yang terdiri  dari:
a. rumah sakit;
b. pusat kesehatan masyarakat;
c. pusat pelayanan terpadu pemberdayaan perempuan dan anak d. rumah perlindungan trauma center;
e. women crisis centre;
f. badan penasehat pembinaan dan pelestarian perkawinan;  g. kepolisian;
h. kejaksaan;
i. pengadilan;
j. kementerian agama; dan/atau
k. organisasi bantuan hukum;

translated_text:
Article 25
Complaint services as referred to in Article 23 paragraph (3) letter a may be coordinated by UPTD PPA with related agencies consisting of:
a. hospitals;
b. community health centers;
c. integrated service centers for women and children empowerment d. trauma center shelters;
e. women crisis centres;
f. advisory board for marriage guidance and preservation;
g. police;
h. prosecutor's office;
i. courts;
j. ministry of religious affairs; and/or
k. legal aid organizations;

Article 27
(1) Health rehabilitation as referred to in Article 23 paragraph (3) letter b constitutes efforts that include the following aspects:
a. promotive, improving so that health status continues to increase;
b. preventive, preventing from contracting diseases;
c. curative, curing a person from physical and psychological illness;
d. rehabilitative, maintaining so that a person who has not fully recovered can return to their original fitness.
(2) Health rehabilitation as referred to in paragraph (1) is carried out comprehensively, accessible 24 (twenty-four) hours, with quality and conducted in accordance with health service standards.
(3) Women and Children victims of acts of violence have the right to free health services, including:
a. medical services;
b. medicolegal services;
c. psychosocial counseling; and
d. Visum et Repertum.
(4) Further provisions regarding the procedures for implementing health services as referred to in paragraph (3) shall be regulated by Regent Regulation.

text:
Pasal 38
Pembinaan sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 37 huruf a, meliputi: a. tumbuh kembang Anak balita;
b. perlindungan terhadap kesehatan reproduksi remaja;
c. pendewasaan usia perkawinan;
d. pengaturan kelahiran; dan
e. meningkatkan kualitas kesehatan ibu hamil dan menyusui. Pasal 39 Bimbingan sebagaimana dimaksud Pasal 37 huruf b meliputi: a. melakukan penyuluhan peningkatan kualitas hidup perempuan; b. melakukan penyuluhan pranikah.
c. fasilitasi penyelenggaraan pembangunan keluarga;

translated_text:
Article 38
Development as referred to in Article 37 letter a, includes: a. growth and development of toddlers;
b. protection of adolescent reproductive health;
c. maturation of marriage age;
d. birth regulation; and
e. improving the health quality of pregnant and breastfeeding mothers. Article 39 Guidance as referred to in Article 37 letter b includes: a. conducting counseling on improving women's quality of life; b. conducting premarital counseling.
c. facilitation of family development implementation;

text:
Pasal 43
(1) Instansi dan pihak swasta yang menyelenggarakan pelayanan publik  wajib menyediakan ruangan laktasi.
(2) Ruangan laktasi sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) merupakan  ruangan yang layak dan memadai.
(3) Pimpinan Instansi yang tidak menyediakan ruangan laktasi sebagaimana  dimaksud pada ayat (1) dikenakan sanksi administratif berupa : a. teguran tertulis; dan/atau
b. sanksi kepegawaian berdasarkan ketentuan Peraturan Perundang Undangan.
(4) Pihak swasta yang tidak menyediakan ruangan laktasi sebagaimana  dimaksud pada ayat (2) dikenai sanksi administratif berupa: a. peringatan tertulis;
b. pembatasan kegiatan usaha;
c. pembekuan kegiatan usaha;
d. denda administratif; dan/atau
e. pencabutan izin.

translated_text:
Article 43
(1) Government agencies and private parties that provide public services are obligated to provide lactation rooms.
(2) Lactation rooms as referred to in paragraph (1) must be proper and adequate rooms.
(3) Heads of Government agencies who do not provide lactation rooms as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be subject to administrative sanctions in the form of: a. written reprimand; and/or
b. employment sanctions based on the provisions of Laws and Regulations.
(4) Private parties who do not provide lactation rooms as referred to in paragraph (2) shall be subject to administrative sanctions in the form of: a. written warning;
b. restriction of business activities;
c. suspension of business activities;
d. administrative fine; and/or
e. revocation of permit.

text:
Pasal 47
(1) Pemerintah Daerah dalam upaya pemenuhan hak Anak  bertanggungjawab:
a. menetapkan dan melaksanakan kebijakan serta program/kegiatan  pemenuhan hak Anak;
b. menghormati dan menjamin hak asasi setiap Anak dengan tidak  membedakan suku, agama, ras, golongan, jenis kelamin, etnik, budaya  dan bahasa, status hukum Anak, urutan kelahiran Anak, dan kondisi  fisik dan/atau mental;
c. menguatkan dan mengembangkan lembaga penyedia layanan  peningkatan kualitas keluarga dalam mewujudkan hak Anak; d. menjamin Perlindungan, pemeliharaan, dan kesejahteraan Anak  dengan memperhatikan hak dan kewajiban orang tua, wali, atau orang  lain yang secara hukum bertanggung jawab terhadap Anak; e. menyediakan sarana dan prasarana dalam penyelenggaraan  pemenuhan hak Anak;
f. menjamin hak Anak untuk menyampaikan pendapat sesuai dengan  usia dan tingkat kecerdasan Anak;
g. melakukan pengawasan dan pembinaan dalam rangka  penyelenggaraan pemenuhan hak Anak;
h.melakukan kerjasama dengan pihak swasta dan/atau LSM dalam  penyelenggaraan Perlindungan Anak;
(2) Tanggungjawab Pemerintah Daerah dalam upaya Perlindungan Anak  sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dilaksanakan oleh OPD sesuai  dengan tugas dan fungsinya.

translated_text:
Article 47
(1) Regional Government in efforts to fulfill the rights of Children is responsible for:
a. establishing and implementing policies and programs/activities for the fulfillment of Children's rights;
b. respecting and guaranteeing the human rights of every Child without distinguishing ethnicity, religion, race, group, gender, ethnic origin, culture and language, legal status of the Child, birth order of the Child, and physical and/or mental condition;
c. strengthening and developing family quality improvement service provider institutions in realizing Children's rights;
d. guaranteeing the Protection, care, and welfare of Children by taking into account the rights and obligations of parents, guardians, or other persons who are legally responsible for the Child;
e. providing facilities and infrastructure in the implementation of the fulfillment of Children's rights;
f. guaranteeing the right of Children to express opinions in accordance with the age and level of intelligence of the Child;
g. conducting supervision and guidance in the context of implementing the fulfillment of Children's rights;
h. conducting cooperation with private parties and/or NGOs in the implementation of Child Protection;
(2) The responsibility of the Regional Government in efforts for Child Protection as referred to in paragraph (1) is implemented by OPD in accordance with their duties and functions.

text:
Pasal 54
(1) Pemerintah Daerah wajib menyelenggarakan layanan kesehatan yang  komprehensif bagi Anak, agar setiap Anak memperoleh derajat kesehatan  yang optimal sejak dalam kandungan.
(2) Layanan kesehatan yang komprehensif sebagaimana dimaksud pada  ayat (1) meliputi:
a. upaya promotif, preventif, kuratif dan rehabilitatif untuk pelayanan  kesehatan dasar;
b. pembebasan dari beban biaya bagi anak gizi buruk, anak penyandang  disabilitas, anak berkebutuhan khusus, anak yang terinfeksi HIV/  AIDS, pekerja anak, anak korban penyalahgunaan narkotika, alkohol,  psikotropika dan zat adiktif lainnya, anak yang menjadi korban  kekerasan, dan anak korban perdagangan orang;
(3) Pemerintah Daerah, masyarakat, keluarga dan orang tua wajib  mengusahakan agar Anak yang lahir terhindar dari penyakit yang  mengancam kelangsungan hidup dan/atau menimbulkan kecacatan.

translated_text:
Article 54
(1) Regional Governments are obligated to provide comprehensive health services for Children, so that every Child obtains optimal health status from the time they are in the womb.
(2) Comprehensive health services as referred to in paragraph (1) include:
a. promotive, preventive, curative and rehabilitative efforts for basic health services;
b. exemption from cost burden for malnourished children, children with disabilities, children with special needs, children infected with HIV/AIDS, child laborers, child victims of narcotics abuse, alcohol, psychotropic substances and other addictive substances, children who are victims of violence, and child victims of human trafficking;
(3) Regional Governments, communities, families and parents are obligated to ensure that Children who are born are protected from diseases that threaten survival and/or cause disability.

text:
Pasal 55
(1) Upaya promotif pelayanan kesehatan dasar sebagaimana dimaksud dalam  Pasal 54 ayat (2) huruf a ditujukan untuk meningkatkan derajat  kesehatan secara lebih optimal.
(2) Upaya promotif sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dilakukan dengan  memberikan sosialisasi atau penyuluhan kepada masyarakat mengenai  pola hidup sehat yang meliputi:
a. pentingnya air susu ibu ekslusif bagi bayi;
b. pentingnya imunisasi bagi balita;
c. pola hidup bersih;
d. pentingnya makanan bergizi; dan
e. bahaya narkoba dan merokok.
(3) Selain upaya promotif sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (2), Pemerintah  Daerah dapat melakukan kegiatan lain dalam rangka penyeleggaraan  kesehatan.

translated_text:
Article 55
(1) Promotive efforts for basic health services as referred to in Article 54 paragraph (2) letter a are aimed at improving health status more optimally.
(2) Promotive efforts as referred to in paragraph (1) are carried out by providing socialization or counseling to the community regarding healthy lifestyle patterns which include:
a. the importance of exclusive breast milk for infants;
b. the importance of immunization for toddlers;
c. clean living patterns;
d. the importance of nutritious food; and
e. the dangers of narcotics and smoking.
(3) In addition to promotive efforts as referred to in paragraph (2), the Regional Government may carry out other activities in the context of health service provision.

text:
Pasal 56
(1) Upaya preventif pelayanan kesehatan dasar sebagaimana dimaksud dalam  Pasal 54 ayat (2) huruf a ditujukan untuk mencegah terjadinya penyakit  atau permasalahan kesehatan.
(2) Upaya sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dilakukan dengan: a. mewajibkan pada ibu untuk pemberian ASI ekslusif pada bayi sampai  usia 6 (enam) bulan;
b. pemberian imunisasi dan vitamin gratis pada bayi dan balita; c. pemberian makanan bergizi kepada balita dari keluarga kurang  mampu;
d. mengoptimalkan peran posyandu untuk pelayanan kesehatan bagi ibu  dan balita;
e. melakukan pemeriksaan kesehatan secara berkala;
f. menyediakan sarana sanitasi dan air bersih disetiap sekolah; dan g. menyediakan fasilitas khusus menyusui atau ruangan pojok ASI di  instansi pemerintah atau dunia usaha.

translated_text:
Article 56
(1) Preventive efforts for basic health services as referred to in Article 54 paragraph (2) letter a are aimed at preventing the occurrence of disease or health problems.
(2) The efforts as referred to in paragraph (1) are carried out by: a. obligating mothers to provide exclusive breastfeeding to infants up to 6 (six) months of age;
b. providing free immunization and vitamins to infants and toddlers; c. providing nutritious food to toddlers from underprivileged families;
d. optimizing the role of posyandu for health services for mothers and toddlers;
e. conducting periodic health examinations;
f. providing sanitation facilities and clean water at every school; and g. providing special breastfeeding facilities or breastfeeding corner rooms at government agencies or business entities.

text:
Pasal 59
Pemerintah Daerah wajib menyelenggarakan Kesejahteraan Sosial bagi:  a. Anak yang berhadapan dengan hukum;
b. Anak korban kekerasan yang tereksploitasi secara ekonomi dan seksual, anak terlantar, anak korban penculikan dan anak korban perdagangan  orang;
c. Anak yang tidak mempunyai orang tua dan diasuh oleh pihak atau  keluarga yang tidak mampu;
d. Anak korban bencana alam atau bencana sosial; dan
e. Anak penyandang disabilitas.

translated_text:
Article 59
Regional Governments are obligated to provide Social Welfare for: a. Children in conflict with the law;
b. Child victims of violence who are exploited economically and sexually, neglected children, child victims of kidnapping and child victims of human trafficking;
c. Children who do not have parents and are cared for by parties or families who are unable to provide;
d. Child victims of natural disasters or social disasters; and
e. Children with disabilities.

text:
Pasal 64
(1) Kebijakan pengembangan KLA diarahkan pada pemenuhan hak Anak  yang terbagi dalam 5 (lima) kelompok, meliputi :
a. hak sipil dan kebebasan;
b. lingkungan keluarga dan pengasuhan alternatif;
c. kesehatan dasar dan kesejahteraan;
d. pendidikan, pemanfaatan waktu luang, dan kegiatan budaya; dan e. Perlindungan khusus.
(2) Ketentuan lebih lanjut mengenai kebijakan pengembangan KLA  sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) diatur dengan Peraturan Bupati.

translated_text:
Article 64
(1) The policy for the development of KLA is directed towards the fulfillment of Children's rights which are divided into 5 (five) groups, comprising:
a. civil rights and freedoms;
b. family environment and alternative care;
c. basic health and welfare;
d. education, utilization of leisure time, and cultural activities; and e. Special protection.
(2) Further provisions regarding the policy for the development of KLA as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be regulated by Regent Regulation.

text:
Pasal 65
(1) Dalam rangka efektifitas pelaksanaan kebijakan KLA di Daerah dibentuk  Gugus Tugas KLA.
(2) Pembentukan dan susunan keanggotaan Gugus Tugas KLA ditetapkan  dengan Keputusan Bupati.
(3) Bupati menetapkan kepala Bappeda sebagai Gugus Tugas KLA dan  kepala OPD yang membidangi pemberdayaan perempuan sebagai  sekretaris Gugus Tugas KLA;
(4) Gugus Tugas KLA sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1), mempunyai  tugas pokok:
a. mengkoordinasikan pelaksanaan kebijakan dan pengembangan KLA; b. melakukan sosialisasi, advokasi dan komunikasi informasi dan edukasi  kebijakan KLA;
c. mengumpulkan data dasar pengembangan KLA;
d. melakukan analisis kebutuhan yang bersumber dari data dasar; e. melakukan deseminasi data dasar;
f. menentukan fokus dan prioritas program dalam mewujudkan KLA,  yang disesuaikan dengan potensi daerah;
g. menyusun rencana aksi daerah Kota Layak Anak 5 (lima) tahunan dan  mekanisme kerja; dan
h. melakukan monitoring, evaluasi dan pelaporan paling sedikit 1 (satu)  tahun sekali.

translated_text:
Article 65
(1) In order to ensure the effectiveness of the implementation of CFC policy in the Region, a CFC Task Force shall be established.
(2) The establishment and membership composition of the CFC Task Force shall be determined by Regent's Decree.
(3) The Regent shall appoint the head of Bappeda as the CFC Task Force and the head of the Regional Apparatus Organization responsible for women's empowerment as secretary of the CFC Task Force;
(4) The CFC Task Force as referred to in paragraph (1), shall have the following main duties:
a. coordinating the implementation of policies and development of CFC; b. conducting socialization, advocacy and communication of information and education on CFC policy;
c. collecting baseline data for CFC development;
d. conducting needs analysis based on baseline data; e. conducting dissemination of baseline data;
f. determining the focus and priority of programs in realizing CFC, which shall be adjusted to regional potential;
g. preparing a 5 (five) year Child Friendly City regional action plan and work mechanism; and
h. conducting monitoring, evaluation and reporting at least once every 1 (one) year.
